034 "-5" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535472 true] [17592186350900 1111 #uuid "651a33da-472b-5998-a25d-caef0ae15022" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350902 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1089 "q-344033" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1100 "Consider the section of the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1$ that lies in the first quadrant.  Given that $x=x(t),$ $y=y(t),$  and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ on the ellipse at the point where $y=3,$ find the value of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1113 #uuid "ca10406f-7159-5346-a4b9-45702956e5e0" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350901 1145 "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2x}{16})+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2y}{25}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, substituting the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ and $y=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{2x}{16})+3\\cdot (\\frac{2(3)}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{18}{25} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also want to substitute for $x,$ but we are not given this value. However, we can find it by substituting $y=3$ into the equation of the ellipse.  \n\nAt the point where $y=3,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{3}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{9}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{16}{25} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{256}{25} \\\\ x & =\\frac{16}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used $x>0$ since we're only interested in the first quadrant. \n\nFinally, substituting $x=\\frac{16}{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{18}{25} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}(\\frac{16}{5})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{18}{25} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{18}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{18}{25}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350903 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350904 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1041 "field-1" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350903 13194139535472 true] [17592186350902 1110 #uuid "38878df5-2dfd-587d-93e5-6898cfd04772" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350903 1034 "-\\frac{9}{5}" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535472 true] [17592186350903 1111 #uuid "87214a7c-d1a1-5776-9383-d77e90fa3915" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350904 1034 "0" 13194139535472 true] [17592186350904 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535472 true] [17592186350904 1111 #uuid "db16fb51-b7ba-56b4-acb2-c24032479eb2" 13194139535472 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-115951" 17592186350830 "q-115951/selection" 17592186350831 "q-115951/selection/7a1faa903ae46b0a3e4acf78c14a9880b73ef464bcd4b78c3e7a703c6538af45" 17592186350832 "q-115951/selection/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" 17592186350833